SVA/macro/preproc indent robustness; regression demos 4-8

Defects found on the real UVM 1.2 tree and on SVA- and macro-heavy
code, all fixed and pinned by new golden demos:

1. A bare group/block close right after an `endif/`ifdef (endfunction,
   endtask, end, endcase, endclass) closes something opened OUTSIDE the
   conditional region, but the engine aligned it with the `ifdef - the
   endfunction of uvm_component.svh do_print and 8 more library sites
   sat one level too deep. The previous-line resolution is now
   transparent through the region: prev1 resolves to the code before
   the matching `ifdef and the close dedents normally. Statements
   after `endif keep the old alignment.

2. An assignment pattern's closing brace preceded by whitespace
   (= '{ min, max, stride }) was not neutralized, leaving an orphan
   block-stop that dedented the following line by a level. The rule
   now allows spaces between the operand and the closing brace.

3. A macro call in the MIDDLE of a line (else `uvm_error(...) or
   if (x) `uvm_info(...), written without a trailing ';') classified
   as a bare control keyword, indenting the next statement one level
   too deep. The macro name now injects a ';' so the line classifies
   as exec; line-leading macros keep the whole-line-to-';' rule.

4. A macro CALL line after an `ifdef was excluded from the
   preprocessor-continuation rules by the leading backtick, so it
   never took the ifdef-body +1 and sat flush with the directive.
   Only real directives are excluded now; macro call lines align and
   dedent like any statement.

Tests: golden demos 4-8. Demo 4: closes after `endif (guarded by
mid-function endif cases). Demo 5: UVM 1.2 excerpt brace shapes
(ternary concat, continuation '{', call-arg '({"str"' with ')' before
the closing brace, assignment pattern, inside-sets, \n in strings).
Demo 6: labeled join/endcase/endclass after `endif, nested conditionals.
Demo 7: advanced SVA - labeled assertions with action blocks, cover
property, expect, multi-line sequence operators, properties with
formal args, nested assertions, bind. Demo 8: SVA mixed with macros -
macro-generated assertions, else-arm macro actions (single/multi-line,
in begin/end), multi-line bind port lists with macro connections,
`ifdef'd bind macros. Full UVM 1.2 tree (145 files) re-verified:
golden, fold, syntax and indent idempotency all pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
